#
# SCOPE
# -----
# IN-CONTRACT LOGIC (reproduce exactly):
#   - The boolean predicate: true iff genuine Map, false otherwise.
#   - Strict-boolean return type for ALL inputs.
#   - The tag string compared in the pure path is EXACTLY '[object Map]'
#     (from Object.prototype.toString.call), and isObjectLike guards null/non-object.
#
# CARRIED DATA: none. (No large literal table. The only constants are short
#   inline tag strings such as '[object Map]', reproduced verbatim in BEHAVIOR.)
#
# OUT-OF-CONTRACT / OUT-OF-ENVELOPE (documented, NOT emitted by genInputs,
#   NOT graded — because the oracle codec cannot reconstruct them, so any stored
#   `expected` would be un-reproducible):
#   - Map SUBCLASS instances (`new (class extends Map)()`): real package -> true,
#     but codec carries a Map only as a plain `new Map(entries)`. OUT.
#   - Plain object / Set / anything with a FORGED Symbol.toStringTag === 'Map':
#     active path -> false, fallback path -> true (they DISAGREE). Not codec-
#     carryable (codec stores no symbol-keyed props). OUT.
#   - `Object.create(Map.prototype)`: active -> false, fallback -> true. Not
#     codec-carryable. OUT.
#   - Proxy wrapping a Map, or a Proxy faking toStringTag: active -> false. Not
#     codec-carryable. OUT.
#   - Cross-realm Map (e.g. from a vm context): not codec-carryable. OUT.
#   - functions: real package -> false, but NOT codec-faithful (functions do not
#     survive JSON.stringify(encode(args))). OUT — documented FALSE.
#   - Symbols: real package -> false, NOT codec-faithful. OUT — documented FALSE.
#   - WeakMap: real package -> false (its tag is '[object WeakMap]' and it lacks
#     [[MapData]]); but WeakMap is NOT codec-carryable (no `{__t:'weakmap'}` tag).
#     OUT — documented FALSE.
